    "ss_home_faq_giy86J": {
      "type": "ss-home-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_j68aBc": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much data do I get with the Netherlands eSIM from $1.45?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM starts at $1.45 and offers several prepaid data allowances to accommodate different travel needs. Available options include 1GB valid for 7 days, 3GB valid for either 15 or 30 days, 5GB and 10GB valid for 30 days, and 20GB valid for 30 days. You can also choose a 50GB package with either 30 or 180 days of validity. Your ideal allowance depends on how often you use navigation, messaging, social media, email, and other online services while traveling. Compare the available packages before purchasing to find a suitable balance between data volume, validity, and cost."
          }
        },
        "question_bQJB69": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long is the Netherlands eSIM data plan valid for?",
            "answer": "The validity of your eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM depends on the data package you select. The available options include a 1GB plan valid for 7 days, 3GB plans valid for 15 or 30 days, and 5GB, 10GB, and 20GB plans valid for 30 days. Travelers requiring connectivity over a longer period can also choose a 50GB package with 180 days of validity. Consider your arrival and departure dates when selecting a plan, especially if you are visiting for an extended holiday or business assignment. The validity period determines how long you can use the purchased allowance. Review the current package options on our Netherlands eSIM page before placing your order."
          }
        },
        "question_BaANgt": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I top up my Netherlands eSIM if I run out of data?",
            "answer": "Yes, eSIMnow lists top-ups as available for its standard Netherlands eSIM. If you use your allocated data before your trip ends, you can add more data rather than necessarily purchasing and installing an entirely new eSIM. This is useful when unexpected activities increase your internet consumption, such as using navigation more frequently, sharing photos, or handling additional work online. Your original package's validity and the applicable top-up conditions are important, so check your order details before adding data. It is also worth monitoring your consumption throughout your stay to avoid running out unexpectedly. Visit our Netherlands eSIM page to review the available package information and prepare for your trip."
          }
        },
        "question_RVKMRA": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does this eSIM work anywhere else in the EU, or only the Netherlands?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM is designed specifically for use in the Netherlands, rather than providing coverage throughout the European Union. Although the Netherlands is part of the EU, purchasing this country-specific package does not automatically give you mobile data access in neighboring destinations such as Germany, Belgium, or France. If your itinerary includes several European countries, consider choosing a regional Europe eSIM that explicitly covers your destinations. This can be more convenient than purchasing separate country-specific plans for every stop. Before buying, check the coverage details of each option against your travel itinerary. Explore our available regional plans if you expect to cross borders during your European trip."
          }
        },
        "question_he3y6z": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the Netherlands eSIM support calls and SMS?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM is a data-only plan, so it does not include traditional cellular voice calls or SMS messages. You can, however, use its mobile data connection with compatible internet-based communication applications to exchange messages and make calls. Services such as WhatsApp may be useful for contacting family, friends, or colleagues, provided the application is accessible and the recipient can also communicate through it. If you need to receive conventional text messages or make calls through your current number, check whether your regular SIM can remain active alongside the eSIM. Remember that using your primary SIM for calls or data may involve charges from your home carrier."
          }
        },
        "question_8xNmr6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which networks does this eSIM connect to in the Netherlands?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM lists three supported local networks: Vodafone 5G, KPN 5G, and Odido 5G. These networks allow compatible devices to access mobile data in the Netherlands without requiring you to purchase a physical local SIM card. Your actual connection will depend on local coverage, your device, network congestion, and whether 5G service is available where you are. A 5G network listing does not guarantee that every location will have a 5G signal or that your phone will always connect at that speed. Before purchasing, confirm that your device supports eSIM technology and is carrier-unlocked. Check our Netherlands product page for the latest technical specifications."
          }
        },
        "question_JmJyWQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I be charged roaming fees while using this eSIM?",
            "answer": "The eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM is a prepaid travel data plan designed to help you avoid unexpected international data roaming charges from your regular mobile carrier. You purchase a defined data allowance upfront and use it within the plan's supported coverage area, giving you better visibility into your connectivity costs. The plan is advertised without hidden roaming fees. However, charges from your existing mobile provider may still apply if your primary SIM uses roaming services while you travel. To reduce this risk, select the Netherlands eSIM as your mobile data line and disable data roaming on your regular SIM. Check your phone's settings before departure to avoid accidental use of your home carrier's data allowance."
          }
        },
        "question_TdxrxN": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I use this eSIM for mobile hotspot or tethering?",
            "answer": "Yes, the eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM supports mobile tethering and hotspotting, enabling you to share your phone's internet connection with compatible devices. This can be convenient when you need to connect a laptop for work, access documents on a tablet, or get another device online while traveling. The data consumed by connected devices counts toward your purchased allowance, so activities such as video streaming, software updates, and large downloads can use data quickly. Your phone must support hotspot functionality, and the connected device needs to be within the required wireless range. Before traveling, check your expected usage and choose an appropriate data package. Review our Netherlands eSIM options to find an allowance suited to your devices and itinerary."
          }
        },
        "question_wyDQNT": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How soon should I activate the eSIM before my trip?",
            "answer": "You can purchase the eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM up to 180 days before activation, giving you flexibility to organize your travel connectivity well in advance. After you buy the e-SIM, you can follow the supplied instructions to install the eSIM on your compatible phone before departure. The plan is designed to activate when the eSIM links with a network that is supported upon arrival in the Netherlands, helping you prepare without necessarily starting your data validity period at home. Follow the activation instructions provided with your order, as installation and activation are separate steps. Check that your phone is compatible and carrier-unlocked before traveling. Preparing these details in advance makes it easier to get connected when you reach your destination."
          }
        },
        "question_PyCNxn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is my phone compatible with the Netherlands eSIM?",
            "answer": "To use the eSIMnow Netherlands eSIM, your device must be able to support e-SIM technology and generally be carrier-unlocked. Many newer iPhone and Android models offer eSIM functionality, but compatibility varies by device model, regional version, and manufacturer specifications. Do not assume that every phone from a particular brand supports eSIM simply because newer models do. Before purchasing, use the device compatibility checker linked on our Netherlands product page to verify your specific phone. It is also helpful to confirm that your device can access its SIM settings and install an eSIM using the supplied instructions. Checking compatibility before departure helps you avoid installation difficulties and prepares you to connect to mobile data during your Netherlands trip."
          }
        }
      },
